  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Hosea",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 5,
    "summary": "The kingdoms of Judah and Israel will both fall because of their iniquities.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Hear ye this, O priests; and hearken, ye house of Israel; and give ye ear, O house of the king; for judgment is toward you, because ye have been a snare on Mizpah, and a net spread upon Tabor.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 109,
            "end": 111
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Hosea 5:1",
        "book": "Hosea",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And the revolters are profound to make slaughter, though I have been a rebuker of them all.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 68
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Hosea 5:2",
        "book": "Hosea",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "I know Ephraim, and Israel is not hid from me: for now, O Ephraim, thou committest whoredom, and Israel is defiled.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 91,
            "text": "Hosea 9:1."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 93,
            "end": 96
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Hosea 9:1.",
            "prettyString": "Hosea 9:1",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "hosea",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 9,
                    "end": 9,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 1,
                        "end": 1
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Hosea 5:3",
        "book": "Hosea",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "They will not frame their doings to turn unto their God: for the spirit of whoredoms is in the midst of them, and they have not known the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 4,
            "text": "HEB Their behavior does not permit them to return to their God."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 85,
            "end": 87
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Hosea 5:4",
        "book": "Hosea",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And the pride of Israel doth testify to his face: therefore shall Israel and Ephraim fall in their iniquity; Judah also shall fall with them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Hosea 5:5",
        "book": "Hosea",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "They shall go with their flocks and with their herds to seek the Lord; but they shall not find him; he hath withdrawn himself from them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 108,
            "end": 117,
            "text": "D&C 101:7 (7–8)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 95,
            "end": 99
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Hosea 5:6",
        "book": "Hosea",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "They have dealt treacherously against the Lord: for they have begotten strange children: now shall a month devour them with their portions.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 101,
            "end": 106,
            "text": "IE Within a month they and their property shall be destroyed."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Hosea 5:7",
        "book": "Hosea",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Blow ye the cornet in Gibeah, and the trumpet in Ramah: cry aloud at Beth-aven, after thee, O Benjamin.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "HEB shofar, or ram’s horn."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 33
          },
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 68
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Hosea 5:8",
        "book": "Hosea",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Ephraim shall be desolate in the day of rebuke: among the tribes of Israel have I made known that which shall surely be.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Hosea 5:9",
        "book": "Hosea",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "The princes of Judah were like them that remove the bound: therefore I will pour out my wrath upon them like water.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 57,
            "text": "HEB boundary marker. Deut. 19:14; Job 24:2; Prov. 22:28."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 68
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Hosea 5:10",
        "book": "Hosea",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Ephraim is oppressed and broken in judgment, because he willingly walked after the commandment.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 73,
            "end": 94,
            "text": "OR after filth."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 10
          },
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 24
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Hosea 5:11",
        "book": "Hosea",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore will I be unto Ephraim as a moth, and to the house of Judah as rottenness.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 14
          },
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 19
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Hosea 5:12",
        "book": "Hosea",
        "chapter": 5,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "When Ephraim saw his sickness, and Judah saw his wound, then went Ephraim to the Assyrian, and sent to king Jareb: yet could he not heal you, nor cure you of your wound.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "Jer. 30:14."
          },
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 73,
            "text": "Hosea 12:1 (1–2)."
          },
          {
            "start": 108,
            "end": 113,
            "text": "Hosea 10:6 (5–6)."
          },
          {
            "start": 132,
            "end": 136,
            "text": "Hosea 14:3 (1–3)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 44
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Jer. 30:14.",
            "prettyString": "Jeremiah 30:14",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "jeremiah",
